\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  ahead of polls  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 15:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealer quote, details, background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday continued its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a bid to satisfy high demand for the dollar and keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable ahead of Sunday's parliamentary election. "The National bank is selling (dollars)," said a source at one of the nation's largest banks.  \par \par \uc2 "Apparently, there is big demand (for dollars) today. There are many buyers -- both large and small banks. But there is no big agitation."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said interbank deals were being struck on Wednesday at 5.0620-5.0630 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar <UAH=> against 5.0615-5.0645 in the previous day's trading.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect high demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hardly ebb after the March 26 election.  \par \par \uc2 "There are no factors which could change this trend," one dealer said. "The elections will pass, but political uncertainty will linger on. The demand on the cash market will press on, while the foreign trade balance is going from bad to worse."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long been committed to keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.06 and defending it against instability linked to the election.  \par \par \uc2 Liberal President Viktor Yushchenko's allies face a big challenge in the contest from a pro-Russian party led by Viktor Yanukovich, the rival he defeated in the 2004 presidential poll and radical former ally Yulia Tymoshenko.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Yushchenko discussed the situation on Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Volodymyr Stelmakh, the presidential press service said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 It said Yushchenko had ordered the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "to launch a wide information campaign in order to stop any speculation about the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... which is of a purely pre-election nature".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent about $1.5 billion in 2006 supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid growing instability -- first sparked in the New Year by parliament sacking the government over a deal sharply raising the price of imported Russian gas.  \par \par \uc2 MARKET-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060322e23m0014g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
