id growing instability -- first sparked in the New Year by parliament sacking the government over a deal sharply raising the price of imported Russian gas.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say inflows of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should rise after the election if parliament, working under new constitutional provisions, proves able to form a coalition able to choose a new prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060321e23l000zh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
