\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine sells dollars, props  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  for 12th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 16 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , propping up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a hotly-contested parliamentary election, sold dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 12th consecutive day.  \par \par \uc2 "Demand exceeded supply today more than was the case on Wednesday, but trades were concluded at more or less the same level thanks to support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Trades were clinched within a range of 5.06-5.063.  \par \par \uc2 "This is a typical pre-election scenario. People are looking for ways within the law to convert their funds into hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer from a large bank.  \par \par \uc2 "Things should calm down after the election."  \par \par \uc2 More than 40 parties are contesting the election to an assembly with greater powers. The winning parties will in effect be entitled for the first time to nominate a prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 The Our Ukraine party backing pro-Western President Viktor Yushchenko lies in second place according to opinion polls, trailing the opposition pro-Russian Regions of Ukraine.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Volodymyr Stelmakh have repeatedly assured markets they see no reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tumble after the election.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said inflows of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will help the market achieve balance if the new parliament is able to form a working majority and choose a government within a reasonable time limit.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already sold around $1.3 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the start of the year. Reserves stood at $19.4 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060316e23g00240\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
