\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine sells dollars as foreigners curb exposure  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 15:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds more comment from dealers)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 11th trading day in a row as some foreigners curbed exposure ahead of a parliamentary election, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Demand could not be met in full on the market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to step in. The volume was rather high. I think about $40 million were sold today," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said demand was fuelled by importers and some foreign investors curbing their exposure ahead of the parliamentary election on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 Over 40 parties are running in the poll to elect an assembly with more powers, with winning groups in effect earning for the first time the right to nominate a prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 The opposition pro-Russian Regions of Ukraine party is leading the polls ahead of a party backing pro-Western President Viktor Yushchenko.  \par \par \uc2 "These are portfolio investors. Some foreigners are selling their treasury notes. But they do not convert the entire amount into dollars. They are also buying corporate and municipal bonds," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko this week pledged the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain stable after the poll.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts from Ukraine's fourth-largest bank Ukrsotsbank expected a hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow to the market and an increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as soon as April.  \par \par \uc2 "Such a situation is typical ahead of the elections," they said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 "But already in April the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will see a splash of dollars from exporters and non-resident investors, which will replenish the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves to start-of-year levels."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already sold around $1.3 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the start of the year. Reserves stood at $19.4 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060315e23f001g0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
