\par\par \b \uc2 Foreigners cut Ukraine debt investment by $192 mln  \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 13 (Reuters) - Foreign portfolio investors have cut their holdings in Ukrainian government domestic debt by $192 million since the start of the year, Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, was quoted on Monday as saying. Business daily Ekonomicheskiye Izvestiya said non-residents were withdrawing funds as they wanted to close their positions at the current \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to the dollar before a parliamentary election on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> is traded at about 5.06 to the dollar.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in March to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cover demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fuelled by increasing political instability before the polls.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells dollars at 5.06 and has so far spent around $120 million in March.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov told Reuters earlier this month that non-residents' holdings of government debt stood at about $1.2 billion.  \par \par \uc2 He said last week there was no reason to speak about capital flight, and he saw no threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine is electing a parliament this month with more constitutional powers effectively giving the winning parties the right to nominate the prime minister and most ministers.  \par \par \uc2 Opinion polls have showed so far that none of the 45 parties running will win an outright majority and coalition talks will be required.  \par \par \uc2 Leading opinion polls is the pro-Russian Regions of Ukraine party, led by Viktor Yanukovich, who was defeated by President Viktor Yushchenko in the 2004 presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-DEBT|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060316e23d001g0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
