\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c.bank defends  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  amid poll jitters  \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 14:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the ninth trading day running on Monday to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a flight into hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fuelled by uncertainty ahead of parliamentary polls on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the mood was nervous, with ordinary people as well as some investors fearing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lose value in the wake of the hotly-contested elections.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling ... People are leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They are converting their deposits into dollars," one dealer said. "Everything is directly linked to the election."  \par \par \uc2 The elections are the first public test for President Viktor Yushchenko's administration after his first year in power following the Orange Revolution.  \par \par \uc2 Many voters appear to be disappointed.  \par \par \uc2 A pro-Russian opposition party, Regions of Ukraine, leads the opinion polls. Analysts say, however, that it is unlikely to get enough votes to win a majority, making a coalition likely.  \par \par \uc2 The pro-presidential party Our Ukraine, and a bloc led by former Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko, who has fallen out with Yushchenko, are in second and third places, polls show.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily this month and has already spent over $120 million propping up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  since August 2005 at a rate of 5.06 to the dollar -- the rate at which it was selling dollars on Monday as well.  \par \par \uc2 Ukrainians, many of whom lost their life-savings due to hyper-inflation and monetary reforms in the mid-1990s, see the dollar as a safe haven at times of political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 Some foreign investors may also be curbing their exposure.  \par \par \uc2 Ukrsotsbank said in a statement it expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slide after the poll.  \par \par \uc2 "The Ukrainian population has started to purchase hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more actively ahead of the parliamentary elections," the bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Local media reports said foreign portfolio investors have cut their holdings in government domestic debt by $192 million since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates non-residents' holdings of government debt at about $1.2 billion. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said last week it was too early to speak about capital flight, adding that they saw no threat to the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said deals were done at between 5.0602-5.0620 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar. "Demand is not that big to break this barrier," one said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060313e23d0013j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\pic