\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars for 5th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 15:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealers' comments)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the fifth straight day on Monday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the move was probably in response to a large buying order for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the market was on the whole balanced.  \par \par \uc2 "I do not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling a lot today. The market was practically balanced. It is likely that a large bank come out and was not able to cover its big volume on the market," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said deals were concluded at 5.059/5.065 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling in recent days, but there is no trend for much larger demand. I think a similiar situation will remain in the coming days. I do not see any factors to pressure the market," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, reiterated the bank's stand that there was no reasons for a \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation.  \par \par \uc2 "We should bear in mind that net \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves are steadily higher than cash \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply in circulation," Shapovalov said in an interview with the weekly Business.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is able to cover any demand to exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  into hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Against this background, rumours of an immintent \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation are highly exaggerated."  \par \par \uc2 Demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being driven by political uncertainty ahead of the parliamentary election on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $100 million in its nearly daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of March.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves slipped to $18.269 billion as of February 28 compared with $18.582 billion at the end of the previous month.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it had spent $179 million on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February and about $1 billion in January. The reserves stood at $19.4 billion as of Jan. 1.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060306e23600182\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
