\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars for 3rd day running  \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quote, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday for the third trading day in a row, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has pledged to maintain financial stability ahead of a March 26 parliamentary election, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly since the start of the year to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cover demand from importers, foreign investors and an unsettled population.  \par \par \uc2 "The market was very narrow today. But demand was still a bit higher. Some people were waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come out," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Deals were done at around 5.0605-5.0650 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar on Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh has said this week the bank was ready to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5-5.06 to the dollar even if demand for the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose during the campaign.  \par \par \uc2 He has predicted the bank would be able to maintain a steady level of reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves stood at $19.4 billion as of Jan. 1. The bank has sold around $1 billion to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in January and February.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine will hold the parliamentary election this month and a new chamber will have more powers and a right to form the government and name the prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 The country is also gripped by a constitutional uncertainty since a New Year deal sharply increasing the price of imported Russian gas prompted parliament to dismiss the government. President Viktor Yushchenko ignored the assembly's move.  \par \par \uc2 Several ministers have taken an official leave to concentrate on the campaigning.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060302e2320016i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
