\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank sells dollars for 2nd straight day  \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 15:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second straight day on Wednesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to large purchases of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by big banks, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the purchases could be linked to uncertainties ahead of Ukraine's March 26 parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone is buying hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Big banks are making especially large purchases," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said most deals were being clinched on the interbank market between 5.062 and 5.065.  \par \par \uc2 "I doubt any deals were made at 5.06. Sales were proceeding at higher rates," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting to calm uncertainty linked to the election, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly throughout January, selling dollars at 5.06 to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sinking at one point to 5.19, that cost the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  about $1 billion.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  became more infrequent last month.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh earlier said the bank was ready to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5-5.06 to the dollar even if demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose during the campaign.  \par \par \uc2 "Of course, we will support it. That is what our reserves are for," Stelmakh said.  \par \par \uc2 He predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be able to maintain its current level of reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe that on the whole, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's balance (in interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will be positive," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "Over the year, the level could dip, but reserves will then be replenished. The economy is only beginning to warm up after a winter slowdown."  \par \par \uc2 The election is taking place under new constitutional provisions effectively giving parties forming a majority in the chamber the right to name the prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine has in any case been plunged into constitutional uncertainty since a New Year deal sharply increasing the price of imported gas prompted parliament to dismiss the government.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko ignored the assembly's move.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060301e2310017s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
