\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank sells dlrs as election approaches  \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2006\par 16:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to correct imbalances caused by increased demand for dollars ahead of next month's parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 It was the bank's first such sale in a week.  \par \par \uc2 "There was serious demand today," said one dealer. "Volumes have risen significantly in recent days and this was inevitable. There will be more and more people wanting to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as we get closer to the election." Dealers said interbank deals were concluded at 5.062-5.064.  \par \par \uc2 A parliamentary election takes place on March 26 under new constitutional provisions effectively giving parties forming a majority in the chamber the right to name the prime minister.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine has in any case been plunged into constitutional uncertainty since a New Year deal sharply increasing the price of imported gas prompted parliament to dismiss the government.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko ignored the assembly's move after which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in January, selling dollars -- about $1 billion - at 5.06 to prop the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped as low as 5.19 at one point.  \par \par \uc2 It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only five times in February.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Tuesday's trend was unlikely to change ahead of the poll.  \par \par \uc2 "I think deals will be somewhere in the range of 5.06-5.07," said one dealer. "But no higher if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays its role and keeps the situation free of tension."  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action would play a key role in the market mood as would pre-election developments.  \par \par \uc2 The tense 2004 presidential election, marked by mass "Orange Revolution" rallies, destabilised the market, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  obliged to sell $2.5 billion of its reserves over two months -- about 20 percent of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060228e22s001ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
