\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , sells dollars  \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2006\par 15:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details, comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday after a two-week pause, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they believed the bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since February 6, sold dollars to a major importer.  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly throughout last month, selling dollars at 5.06 to prop the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against uncertainty linked to a March 26 parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 "It would appear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was covering demand from a large importer unable to find the required sums on the market," one market participant said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded throughout the day at about 5.057/5.06.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflected specific market conditions rather than a trend.  \par \par \uc2 "The reasons for strong dollar demand that we saw in January are not present at the moment," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no reason over the next week to see the market slip beyond 5.06. It's difficult to say whether there will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tomorrow, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would appear able to meet demand today or in the near future."  \par \par \uc2 The head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's council, Valery Heyets, said last week the bank stood by its forecast of 5.0-5.2 for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 2006 despite a forecast worsening of the trade balance to a $2 billion deficit.  \par \par \uc2 A surplus of $300 million is expected to be posted for 2005.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $1 billion from its reserves in January to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady ahead of the election to a parliament with expanded powers.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine remains gripped by a constitutional deadlock prompted by parliament's sacking of the government in January in response to the signing of a deal providing for sharp increases in the price of gas imported from Russia.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060221e22l0013k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
