\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine C.Bank buys dollars for 12th straight day  \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2006\par 15:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds comment, background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 12th straight day to guard against instability amid pre-election political turmoil.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they were surprised at the bank's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the market was relatively balanced.  \par \par \uc2 "I frankly don't know why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, or even yesterday or the day before that," said one dealer. "You could have bought dollars more cheaply than 5.06 yesterday. The level is practically the same today."  \par \par \uc2 Hit by turbulence linked to a March parliamentary election, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank at one point in mid-January to 5.19. Continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases have since kept it steady.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine has been gripped by a constitutional crisis since parliament sacked the government in response to the conclusion of a Jan. 4 deal to import gas from Russia at higher prices.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko has ignored the move. Talks are in progress on agreements needed to underpin the accord.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted now for only 10-20 percent of sales on the market, whereas it covered nearly all sales earlier in the month. "Supply (of dollars) is a lot better now," said another dealer. "You can now easily get hold of what you need."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since last August been committed to maintaining the dollar at about 5.06. Its first deputy chairman last week said the bank had spent $780 million since the New Year supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers predicted continued balance over the next week.  \par \par \uc2 "Some questions do remain. Everyone is waiting for the election and the gas issue is not settled yet," said one dealer. "But this is not being reflected in trading for the moment. The feeling is the market will remain in balance for this week."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|BNX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060201e2210013v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
