\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars for 10th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2006\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds comment, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 30 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, pursuing its bid in a pre-election period to prop the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars at 5.06 for the 10th consecutive trading day.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted despite relative balance in the market, with only minimal variations in rates.  \par \par \uc2 Hit by political turbulence linked to a March parliamentary election, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on the interbank market by mid-afternoon to 5.058/5.0605 against 5.06/5.065 at the opening.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine has been gripped by a constitutional crisis since parliament dismissed the government in response to the conclusion of a Jan. 4 deal to import gas from Russia at higher prices. President Viktor Yushchenko has ignored the move.  \par \par \uc2 "Things were pretty quiet, there wasn't an awful lot of movement," one dealer said. "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to meet just about all the demand. Its action was intended merely to ensure stability."  \par \par \uc2 Another dealer said there was adequate dollar supply.  \par \par \uc2 "But no one wanted especially to sell any cheaper than 5.06 and those able to buy through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unwilling to pay more," he said. "Only those needing quick delivery to close contracts bought at rates more expensive than 5.06."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since last August been committed to maintaining the dollar at about 5.06.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier been linked to sharply declining revenues from exports.  \par \par \uc2 "Supply has risen considerably as many people who had wanted to get more for their dollars hung on to them for a time," said one dealer. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has punished them for their greed. Once it started selling, the rate fell."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had traded at one point as low as 5.19 in mid-January.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060130e21u00180\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
