\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars for 8th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2006\par 13:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from political turbulence, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the eighth trading day running, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling again today. Uncertainty over a gas deal and unresolved political deadlock are plaguing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer said. "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to keep selling until these issues are settled."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily this month to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hit by a constitutional dispute between the government and parliament.  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told Reuters in an interview on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about $780 million from reserves to prop up the sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine is gripped by a constitutional crisis after parliament sacked the government over an expensive gas deal. But President Viktor Yushchenko has refused to recognise the dismissal ahead of a parliamentary election on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 Tensions have calmed this week as parliament is in recess until Feb. 7.  \par \par \uc2 Economists are also worried over uncertainty on Russian natural gas supplies to Ukraine this year.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine and Russia have agreed on gas deliveries for this year, raising the price to $95 per 1,000 cubic metres against $50 previously. But the signing of the agreement to seal the deal was postponed for the second time on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue defending a level of 5.06 to the dollar in the near term until the government announces new macroeconomic forecasts for this year.  \par \par \uc2 "The government has promised to announce the figures in early February. Then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may announce a new forecast for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "Until then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not be much lower but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to help."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said deals were concluded at about 5.065 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, roughly the same as on Wednesday. The average \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is forecast at between 5.00-5.20 to the dollar for 2006.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060126e21q00161\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
