\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-INTERVIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  costs $780 mln  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yuri Kulikov  \par \uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2006\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds latest c. bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent $780 million from its reserves so far this year to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against political instability, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first deputy chairman said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily since the New Year to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hit by a constitutional deadlock pitting parliament against the president and growing tension ahead of a March 26 parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Wednesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the seventh trading day running, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "In recent days the situation on the interbank market has calmed down. Certainly, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to spend $780 million from its reserves on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of the month," Anatoly Shapovalov told Reuters in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $19.395 billion on Dec. 31.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> recovered its losses this week, trading at around 5.06/5.07 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But last week it hit a nine-month low of around 5.20 after parliament sacked the government of Prime Minister Yuri Yekhanurov over a costly gas deal with Russia. President Viktor Yushchenko refused to recognise parliament's move.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said there are no economic reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness and regularly sold dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the level it has defended since last August.  \par \par \uc2 "The market has started to balance due to rising hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows on corresponding accounts and a reduction of domestic demand," Shapovalov said. "The market has calmed down because it sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efficient actions. Yesterday the gap between demand and supply was only $30 million."  \par \par \uc2 "I think the market will stabilise at the level of 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar," Shapovalov said.  \par \par \uc2 LONG-TERM TROUBLES  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also said dollar demand from the cash market had started to diminish.  \par \par \uc2 But they also said unfavourable world markets and higher gas prices would hit exporters, the main driver behind the country's economic growth in the last four years and produce difficulties for a fragile \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the longer term.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should realise there are not only psychological but also economic reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness," a dealer said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to change the rate. It is just a question of time."  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said further developments on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market depended on the fate of the gas supply agreement between Ukraine and Russia.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine and Russia have agreed on gas supplies for this year, raising the price to $95 per 1,000 cubic meters against $50 previously. But the signing of the agreement to seal the deal was postponed for the second time on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Everybody is waiting to see what the gas agreements will be. If 95 dollars for 1,000 cubic metres will remain in force for a year I think there will be no serious volatility on the market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enough reserves. Industrialists and exporters said they can survive under $95," he said. (Additional reporting by Olena Horodetska)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2, INTERVIEW)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060125e21p000xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
