\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars for 5th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2006\par 13:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quote)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fifth trading day running, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 They said confidence had returned to the market after last week's volatility and saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilise thanks to continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support since the start of the year. Deals were concluded around 5.06/5.065 per dollar on Monday compared with about 5.08 per dollar on Friday, they said.  \par \par \uc2 "Demand is slowing down. People have calmed down a bit. (Dollar) supply is also picking up a bit," a dealer said. "The market is returning to its normal balance."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily this month to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been losing ground over a constitutional clash between parliament and President Viktor Yushchenko. Parliament has sacked the government but Yushchenko has refused to recognise the decision.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko was due to address the nation on Monday evening to mark his first year in power.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to a nine-month low last week.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 15 emerging market strategists showed on Friday that any weakness would be shortlived and over by mid-year, thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a presumed return of investor confidence after a parliamentary election on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060123e21n0019m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
