\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c bank sells dollars for 4th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2006\par 14:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth day running.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> regained ground on Friday thanks to continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support this week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to a new nine-month low on Thursday as it has repeatedly since parliament dismissed the government last week.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has promised to continue supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was covering all bids yesterday. It says it will do the same today. It has helped. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting back to normal. It was rising today," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was traded up at about 5.08 to the dollar on Friday compared with 5.10/5.12 at Thursday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told Reuters on Thursday the slide was caused by politics not economics and said the bank was prepared for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to back the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 15 emerging market strategists showed any weakness would be shortlived and over by mid-year, thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a presumed return of investor confidence after a parliamentary election on March 26.  \par \par \uc2 The poll showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 5.07 by end-June, though economists did not rule out the possibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening to 5.25 or 5.30 in the near-term due to pre-election political instability.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine is plagued by a constitutional crisis after parliament's dismissal of the government and President Viktor refusing to accept such a move. Yushchenko and parliament accuse each other of violating the constitution.  \par \par \uc2 Attempts to break the deadlock have produced no results. Parliament closed for its winter recess on Friday and will start a new session on February 7.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060120e21k0014x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
