\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Weakness in Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  seen short-lived  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Toni Vorobyova  \par \uc2 905 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2006\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 20 (Reuters) - Any weakness in Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably be shortlived and should be over by mid-year, thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a return of investor confidence after March general elections, a Reuters poll shows.  \par \par \uc2 The Reuters poll of 15 emerging market strategists showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> at around 5.07 per dollar by end-June even as an increase in gas prices trims Ukraine's economic growth this year and nudges its current account into deficit.  \par \par \uc2 That is only slightly above the 5.05 level to which it was revalued last April and roughly where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It has bought \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  most days since the start of the year, resisting pressure for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after parliament sacked the government over a contentious deal under which \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to pay more for imported Russian gas.  \par \par \uc2 Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to fresh nine-month lows of 5.19/5.20 per dollar on Thursday, with dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had failed to cover all bids. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  then regained ground after a top official told Reuters the bank was ready to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We expect (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to defend the loose dollar peg through this year's turbulent politics, to prevent any possible household panic from becoming self-fulfilling," said Rory MacFarquhar at Goldman Sachs in Moscow.  \par \par \uc2 A sharp weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the dollar could unsettle ordinary Ukrainians who tend to turn to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a safe haven in times of political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 However, the 5.07 median forecast for end June and 5.05 for end-year could mask the potential for a weakening to 5.25 or 5.30 per dollar in the near-term.  \par \par \uc2 Some said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could pick up pace in coming weeks -- with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of over $19 billion the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can afford to be more aggressive.  \par \par \uc2 Even without bolder \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could strengthen once the March 26 parliamentary election is over and market attention returns to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 "Fundamentals relative to the pricing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (suggest that) the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be so much stronger -- about 15 percent at least," said Lars Christensen at Danske Bank in Copenhagen.  \par \par \uc2 ELECION OUTCOME UNCLEAR  \par \par \uc2 Strategists said the election would probably not result in an outright win for any party, but there was no clear consensus in the poll on the most likely coalition formation.  \par \par \uc2 Leading in opinion polls is the Regions Party of Viktor Yanukovich, the rival that liberal President Viktor Yushchenko defeated in the long, bruising 2004 presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 Lying second is a bloc led by Yulia Tymoshenko, Yushchenko's ally during 2004 "Orange Revolution" protests but dismissed as prime minister last September and now running against the president's allies. The pro-presidential Our Ukraine party is in third place.  \par \par \uc2 Despite differences, any two of these could form a coalition. Or whoever wins the most votes may join forces with smaller parties.  \par \par \uc2 "We are going to see fairly unstable governments for some time to come, but I don't think investor sentiment will necessarily be badly affected," said Sonal Desai at DrKW in Milan.  \par \par \uc2 One possible exception could be greater power for Tymoshenko, who has criticised the gas deal and favours policies such as higher social spending which please voters but can seem imprudent to foreign investors, strategists said. The results of the election could to a certain extent affect Ukraine's growth and current account outlook this year.  \par \par \uc2 Overall, the poll forecast growth of 2.5 percent this year -- fractionally up from a 5-year low of 2.4 percent posted last year and compared to 12.1 percent in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 That is based on Ukraine paying Russia $95 per 1,000 cubic meters of gas, up from $50 previously but still well bellow open market rates. Strategists said the gas deal would probably hold as there is little chance of Ukraine negotiating better rates.  \par \par \uc2 One risk, according to Tim Ash at Bear Stearns in London, is that Russia could push for even higher prices.  \par \par \uc2 "If the new government is seen in Moscow as being overly anti-Russia we could well see further attempts to renegotiate from July onwards," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The present deal will push Ukraine's current account into a deficit of 2 percent of GDP this year, the poll showed.  \par \par \uc2 But even if Ukraine had been allowed to continue paying old gas prices, the poll forecast modest growth of 4.5 percent this year and a current account surplus of just 1.0 percent of GDP.  \par \par \uc2 "Even without a natural gas issue, the low growth rate in net exports and low growth in fixed investments will provide low one digit growth rate of the economy," said Alexander Valchyshen at ING Bank Ukraine.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the negative effects on Ukraine's economy this year, the gas deal could eventually prove to be a positive.  \par \par \uc2 "In the long run, the sharp increase in gas prices is actually a positive for the country and holders of its longer-dated Eurobonds, as it improves the chances for an orderly transition to much higher prices for gas in about 5 years' time," said Sergei Voloboev at Credit Suisse in London.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Natalie Harrison)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-POLL|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060120e21k000wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
