\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  after new  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  dip  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Olena Horodetska  \par \uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2006\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fresh dealer comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> after it dropped to a new 9-month low amid political uncertainty, but dealers said it failed to cover all bids.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged to 5.1530/5.1670 to the dollar at 1035 GMT, its lowest point in nine months, compared with 5.1050/5.1150 at the opening.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the level it has been defending since last August.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers said, having failed to meet all bids, the bank and had paved the way for further weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is imposing limits on dollar sales for no clear reason. It gives no explanation," one dealer said. "We are not demanding a \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 5.06 to the dollar. We want clear and transparent rules."  \par \par \uc2 Others said the repeated failure to cover dollar demand might unsettle Ukrainians, who tend to turn to the dollar as a safe commodity in times of political uncertainty.  \par \par \uc2 "Such \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions ... will fuel further demand and, inevitably, a sharp dollar rise on the cash market," said Serhiy Borysov, a deputy chairman at Finance and Credit.  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Arseniy Yatsenyuk said there was no economic basis for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be subject to volatility given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's robust reserves. The reserves grew to $19.4 billion at the end of 2005 from $9.5 billion a year ago.  \par \par \uc2 "We see no economic reasons for any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility," said Yatsenyuk, who was deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 "I am certain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as an independent body, has all instruments to uphold price stability via the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  NEARLY EVERY DAY  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily in January as the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  started losing ground after parliament sacked the government over a contentious gas deal under which Ukraine is to pay more for imported Russian gas.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also suffering from a sharp decrease in export revenues.  \par \par \uc2 Key export sectors -- steel and chemicals -- are struggling with lower global prices for their products, rising competition from producers like China and the steep increase in gas prices.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's main industries are energy-intensive and prices for Russian gas have nearly doubled to about $95 per 1,000 cubic metres under the deal signed in the New Year.  \par \par \uc2 Political uncertainty is compounding the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes less than two months before a parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 Parliament and President Viktor Yushchenko accuse each other of violating the constitution after the government was sacked on the grounds that the gas deal betrayed national interests.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko was chairing a meeting of the National Security and Defence Council on Wednesday. On Thursday, he and his prime minister are to attend a session of parliament.  \par \par \uc2 "The political turmoil is even greater than expected ahead of the election and I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sitting half on the sidelines, just using the bare minimum of its reserves to maintain some kind of order," said Sonal Desai at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \par \par \uc2 "I see the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  bouncing around and maybe weaker in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  time but I do not see it going into freefall." (Additional reporting by Sujata Rao in London)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060118e21i000l4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
