\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  after  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  falls  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2006\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (New story with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 17 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it sank to a new nine-month low.  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times last week on the market as dollar demand, fuelled by declining export revenues and political uncertainty, far outstripped supply.  \par \par \uc2 "As I understand it, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling just the amount required by people -- not in terms of speculation but rather in connection with real contracts," a dealer from a major bank said of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slipped in the space of an hour in morning trading to 5.104/5.1155 from 5.09/5.096.  \par \par \uc2 That level was the lowest since the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at about 5.18 to the dollar in late April 2005. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then engineered a sharp rise of about 3 percent in a single day to a rate of about 5.05.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said demand had outpaced supply by a factor of better than 10 to one before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the imbalance stemmed from a sharp decline in export revenues compared to 2005 levels, with even \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unable to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at previous levels.  \par \par \uc2 They were unwilling to make forecasts on future levels.  \par \par \uc2 "For some banks it should be at 5.10, for others at 5.06," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "But the fact is there are no significant sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , exports are generating no revenue and therefore banks unable to deal with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are buying at a high rate."  \par \par \uc2 PRESSUE FROM POLITICS  \par \par \uc2 Pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensified following parliament's dismissal of the government last week and continuing uncertainty in the campaign leading up to a March 26 parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 Parliament is at odds with President Viktor Yushchenko, with each accusing the other of violating the constitution after last week's vote over a contentious gas deal.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko on Wednesday chairs a meeting of Ukraine's Security and Defence Council devoted to the effects of political factors on the country's social and economic climate.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers suggested further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be required.  \par \par \uc2 "The market will almost certainly open tomorrow at 5.1 and some sort of trend will be established at about 11 a.m., when real sellers, not speculators, appear," said one dealer. "Speculators will be selling at 5.11 early on."  \par \par \uc2 The bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently over the past year, both selling and buying dollars to keep it within a target corridor of 5.0 to 5.06.  \par \par \uc2 But dollar supply exceeded demand through most of 2005, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying up $10.4 billion to bring its end-year reserves to $19.4 billion against $9.5 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 The average \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is forecast at between 5.0 to 5.20 to the dollar for 2006.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060117e21h000nx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
