\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  hits 9-month low, c. bank steps in  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Olena Horodetska  \par \uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2006\par 10:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds S&P report)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell dollars on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to its lowest level since April 2005 following parliament's sacking of the government.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave a lift to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> which had fallen to 5.091/5.098 to the dollar in early trade compared with 5.075/5.0875 per dollar at the opening.  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told Reuters the bank would cover all bids at a rate of 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar, the level it has defended for about 6 months.  \par \par \uc2 "The government resignation caused this jump (in the dollar)," Shapovalov said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But certainly it was selling within its limits for each bank. Probably, some were still unable to cover all their bids," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to regain ground immediately after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , quickly reaching the 5.06 level.  \par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's agency also provided some comfort, reaffirming its ratings on Ukraine, saying that despite relatively bleak economic prospects, low debt levels gave the government flexibility with its budget.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rebound further this week provided the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to support it.  \par \par \uc2 "I do not think the dollar will go higher than 5.07 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  tomorrow. Many will wait for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including us," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKET UNSETTLED  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a tight grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both selling and buying dollars, to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a target corridor of 5.00-5.06. But it stayed out of the market on Tuesday, unsettling dealers.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have repeatedly said there were no economic reasons for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall and vowed to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $19.395 billion at the end of December.  \par \par \uc2 The average \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is forecast at between 5.00-5.20 to the dollar for 2006.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said some demand for dollars came from non-residents withdrawing funds after the finance ministry repaid some \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated government debt. He estimated the demand at about $36 million.  \par \par \uc2 "It is not a major factor and it was expected," he said. "The government resignation is an extraordinary event. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate became the first indicator. (Banks) reacted in a similar way to previous resignations."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said there was also demand for dollars from an unsettled population and from rising hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by oil importers.  \par \par \uc2 Parliament voted on Tuesday to fire the government of Prime Minister Yuri Yekhanurov after Ukraine agreed to pay higher prices for Russian natural gas imports this year.  \par \par \uc2 It was the second government to fall in just over three months and since President Viktor Yushchenko took power after the 'Orange Revolution'.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko said the sacking was unconstitutional and said Yekhanurov would remain Ukraine's premier until the March 26 parliamentary election.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's internationally traded debt steadied on Wednesday after yield premiums widened by around 10 basis points a day earlier. Ukraine's section of the JP Morgan EMBI+ index <UKREMBIP=JPM> was steady at 183 ticks over U.S. Treasuries.  \par \par \uc2 The country's main PFTS <.PFTSI> stock index recovered some losses, inching up by 0.5 percent at Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Natalya Zinets)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060111e21b000k6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
