\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c. bank buys dollars for 2nd straight day  \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2005\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds c. bank comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day in a row, as funds from the record sale of a steel mill hit the market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to buy out hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Kryvorizhstal privatisation at a rate of 5.0 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to buy out this hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the rate which we have been using for purchases since August. That's 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar," Shapovalov told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it is ready to step in on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable following the privatisation from which Ukraine raised $4.8 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Mittal Steel , the world's largest steel producer, won a repeat tender in October to buy 93.02 percent of Kryvorizhstal, a privatisation hailed by analysts as a major success of President Viktor Yushchenko's 10 months in power.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said commercial banks, acting on behalf of Mittal Steel, had already sold $250 million on the market in the last two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying dollars. Everybody seemed to feel the high dollar supply was caused by the Kryvorizhstal sale. The money is either already here or the market is psychologically ready for it," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The new tender in Kryvorizhstal was ordered after courts ruled illegal the plant's initial sale for about $800 million to businessmen with close ties to the previous administration.  \par \par \uc2 Officials have said that half the $4.8 billion is to be paid by the end of the week, with the remainder in December.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued its standard statement saying it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00/5.06 per dollar and set an unlimited volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051122e1bm000z3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
