\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine cbank resumes dollar purchases  \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2005\par 15:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since Oct. 28, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which tightly controls the market, has stayed away from it so far this month. But hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply has grown, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> closer to the psychologically important level of 5.00 to the dollar and forcing the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The bank has been constantly saying it intended to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00-5.06 to the dollar. Today the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slowly moved to about 5.005 and they stepped in," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers reported deals done at about 5.02-5.03 to the dollar in early trade, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to about 5.005/5.015 later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 "It was not clear how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying out but we felt imbalance on the market was not big today. There is not much economic sense to hang on to the dollar at the moment. People expect dollars from Kryvorizhstal's sale," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine sold its largest steel mill Kryvorizhstal for a record amount of $4.8 billion last month to Mittal Steel , the world's biggest steel producer. About a half of that amount is due to be paid this month.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed to help commercial banks handle the sale proceeds which are greater than one month's transactions on Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, as well as promising to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051117e1bh001h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
