\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c. bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , buys dollars  \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2005\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (New story with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it closely controls, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its first such purchase since Oct. 13.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars as there was a big operator offering large amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> had crept up to 5.019/5.021 per dollar in early afternoon trading compared with 5.03/5.045 in the morning and 5.03/5.037 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently keeps the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 5.0 and 5.06 and is committed to an average rate of 5.1 throughout 2005. Its target for 2006 is a corridor ranging from 5.0 to 5.2.  \par \par \uc2 It had earlier issued its standard announcement declaring its readiness to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the prescribed limits and giving the volume of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as unlimited.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stayed out of the market for most of October, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  last on Oct. 13 to buy dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 . From Oct 4-6, the bank sold dollars at 5.06.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise in connection with the landmark sale this week of the Kryvorizhstal steel mill for $4.8 billion by Mittal Steel .  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko's chief of staff, Oleh Rybachuk, added his voice to assurances from ministers that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was well positioned to ensure that the inflow of funds would not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, first deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told Reuters this week the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was standing at an optimal rate and the bank had no intention of revaluing it after the sale.  \par \par \uc2 He said the bank was ready to buy out the full amount to prevent imbalances on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 At the start of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen as undervalued due to robust export revenues and a steady inflow of funds in Ukraine's domestic debt market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by about 3 percent on a single day in April. It has since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both buying and selling hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend its target rate.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051028e1as0014q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
