\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c. bank says may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  at 5.00/5.06/$  \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2005\par 12:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within 5.00 to 5.06 per dollar, and set the indicative volume for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $30 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> rose to 5.015/5.03 per dollar at 0940 GMT compared with 5.03/5.05 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the opening and 5.07/5.09 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar last week.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, a regular feature since September, is meant as a signal that the bank intends to keep the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within clear boundaries. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at 5.06 for three trading days last week as rising imports fuelled demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It stayed away from the market on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 It had been buying dollars regularly for weeks leading up to late September to prevent a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply was set to rise later in the month thanks to the new privatisation tender of the country's largest steel mill Kryvorizhstal later this month and following a successful sovereign Eurobond placement last week.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine will sell Kryvorizhstal on Oct. 24 and is accepting bids until Oct. 17. The government has already received deposits from two interested buyers.  \par \par \uc2 The government sold a 10-year 600 million euro-denominated bond with a coupon of 4.95 percent on Oct. 5.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051011e1ab000qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
