\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars for third day  \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2005\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars for the third straight day at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday as rising imports fuelled demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at more than the $40 million the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier set as its indicative volume.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably sold more than $40 million today. But not all deals will be covered," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to 5.09/5.097 per dollar but recovered to about 5.07/5.075 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its intention to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market with dollar sales.  \par \par \uc2 "After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made the announcement, the quotes came back and people calmed down," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been announcing indicative parameters for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the start of each trading day since August.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday it narrowed the spread for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 5.049/5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar from the 5.00/5.06 it had been announcing for the past two months.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday and Wednesday to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Until mid-September it had been buying dollars to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising.  \par \par \uc2 Before this week's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it last sold dollars on June 24, also at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dollar sales were almost certain to continue, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Demand is big and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to sell every day for now," said one dealer. "Everything goes to cover import contracts. This is a traditional time for energy payments."  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine depends heavily on energy imports, mostly from Russia, and demand for fuel and gas traditionally rises in autumn and winter.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051006e1a6000o1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
