\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine C.Bank sells dollars for second day  \b0\par\par\uc2 126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2005\par 15:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars for the second straight day at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a fall in the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 There was no immediate indication on the volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier stuck to its practice of announcing in advance its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans, putting the indicative volume at $40 million, higher than its usual level.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh said earlier on Wednesday that the bank would "definitely" conduct fresh dollar sales if necessary. The bank had until mid-September been buying dollars for months to guard against a sharp rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051005e1a50016b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
