\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - UPDATE 2-Ukraine c.bank sells dollars for second straight day  \b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2005\par 09:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 In Oct. 5 KIEV story about Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales, please read headline as "Ukraine c.bank sells dollars for second straight day" instead of "Ukraine c.bank buys dollars for second straight day" (correcting to "sells" from "buys").  \par \par \uc2 The story is repeated below.  \par \par \uc2 (adds new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fresh quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second day running on Wednesday and its chairman pledged to proceed with further sales if they were deemed necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank sold dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a fall in the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They said the bank's indicative volume of $40 million in dollar sales -- higher than its usual level -- failed to cover demand.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is not covering demand. Demand exceeded the promised $40 million," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was fetching 5.07 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more in interbank trading against 5.02 at the end of last week.  \par \par \uc2 "Things could go even further tomorrow," said another dealer. "We will almost certainly go through the 5.07/08 level."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh had earlier made it plain the bank, which until mid-September had been buying dollars to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising, was ready to oversee further sales to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady.  \par \par \uc2 "Definitely," Stelmakh said when asked by reporters whether Tuesday's sale of dollars would be repeated if required.  \par \par \uc2 "There is nothing dreadful about any of this. We have to aim for an average rate of 5.10 to the dollar and we haven't yet reached that," he said, referring to the rate set down in the 2005 budget and other official policy documents.  \par \par \uc2 He said Ukrainian money supply had increased in connection with payment of increased social benefits.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  must find its own balance. At the same demand demand is increasing for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were the first in more than three months. Its last purchase dates from Sept. 12.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to allow a major depreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Ukraine entering a long campaign ahead of parliamentary elections next March.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been officially fixed at a rate of about 5.05 since late April after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by about 3 percent in a move that undermined market and public confidence.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has since introduced freer trading rules on the market to allow commercial banks to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same day and make forward deals.  \par \par \uc2 First Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Anatoly Shapovalov, addressing a banking forum, urged consumers not to panic.  \par \par \uc2 Supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, would rise sharply after Ukraine's planned Eurobond issue this month totalling 600 million euros and the new selloff on Oct 24 of the giant Kryvorizhstal steel mill.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051005e1a5000g3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
