\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  slides, c. bank stays clear  \b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2005\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , new quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed clear of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday despite a slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after end of the quarter book-closing and fears over deteriorating trade figures generated demand for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> was traded at 5.049/5.053 to the dollar on Friday down from 5.025/5.032 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed clear today. It can reappear on the market when the rate will be at about 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar. That was the level when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last sold dollars to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which keeps tight control over Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, last sold dollars on June 24. In July and in August, it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily to buy out dollars and prevent any sharp upward movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Since mid-September it has stayed out of a market made more balanced by freer rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at 5.00/5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar and set the indicative volume at $10 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has announced the same parameters for most of the month.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  might slide to 5.06 to the dollar next week.  \par \par \uc2 "Today, clients were not ready to buy more expensive dollars. But they will be ready tomorrow. In several days we will creep up to 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to come out then," a dealer said. "They didn't allow revaluation. They will certainly not allow devaluation."  \par \par \uc2 Even the slightest volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a sensitive issue in Ukraine where millions lost life savings to hyper-inflation and botched monetary reforms in the early 1990s.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sliding due to lower revenues from exporters, who are suffering from deteriorating world markets for steel and chemicals, Ukraine's major exports.  \par \par \uc2 "There are no export revenues, but imports are rising. It should be covered," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Government officials have said the trade balance may plunge into deficit this year due to slowing exports and deteriorating world market conditions. Last year, the trade surplus reached a record $3.676 billion.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050930e19u000qx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgo