\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank stays out, market seen balanced  \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2005\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds dealers comment, no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed clear of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday as dealers said new rules making it easier for them to do business were likely to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action in the long-term.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps tight control over the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly daily to buy out dollars and curb any sharp movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Yielding to pressure from foreign experts and government officials, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  approved new rules for the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market effective last week, allowing banks to make forward deals and buy and sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same trading day.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the steps have started to yield results.  \par \par \uc2 "Finally, we can buy and sell on the same day. It is helping a lot," a dealer at a large Ukrainian bank said.  \par \par \uc2 "The market was in a very narrow range today, deals were done between 5.012 and 5.015 (\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar). There were many buyers and sellers."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now announces parameters for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the start of the trading day. On Tuesday, it said it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.00/5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar and set the indicative volume at $10 million. It announced the same indicators and bought dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes to cut the frequency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Printing \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase dollars, last month it bought $735.9 million on the market compared with $397.3 million in July.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from late April have sought to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable and defend exporters, the driving force behind the country's economic recovery in the last three years. In April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate by about 3 percent in a single stroke.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been widely seen as undervalued due to robust exports and a steady inflow of funds into the debt market.  \par \par \uc2 But Acting Finance Minister Viktor Pynzenyk, still performing his duties after the government was dismissed last week, said on Monday there were no grounds to expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050913e19d001el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
