\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c. bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , 5.0/dlr rate unchanged  \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2005\par 14:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an unchanged rate from the previous session, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market tightly and has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily over the last month trying to avoid sharp upward movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has set the volume for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $30 million.  \par \par \uc2 "There are again loads of dollars on the market today. We feel the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be buying even more than $30 million," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine has been flooded with dollars this year due to strong exports, a good grain harvest and an inflow of foreign funds into the domestic debt market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by about 3 percent in a single stroke at the end of April which shook market confidence badly and hurt exporters. Since that time it has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market nearly daily to curb any sharp upward movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $735.9 million on the interbank market in August compared with $397.3 million in July, boosting its gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $14.451 billion as of Aug. 31.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under increasing pressure in recent weeks from President Viktor Yushchenko, dealers and the International Monetary Fund who want it to ease its tight grip on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transations.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said they wanted to cut the frequency of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and removed some limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published new rules allowing forward trading for the first time and enabling commercial banks to buy and sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same trading day.  \par \par \uc2 However, dealers were sceptical, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened some other requirements.  \par \par \uc2 "There is too much regulation on the market. It will not be easy even with new rules," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The rules are due to go into effect on Sept 9.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050906e196001ab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
